  "status": "Artifact implementation and focused kernel/runtime acceptance passed; root-owned live caller/publication/retrieval composition and M5.2 delivery acceptance remain active.",
  "specs": [
    "\u00a7FS-host-boundary.artifacts",
    "\u00a7FS-host-boundary.transport",
    "\u00a7FS-host-boundary.publication",
    "\u00a7AR-host-boundary.interfaces",
    "\u00a7AR-host-boundary.acceptance"
  ],
  "claim": "The actual total artifact validator derives typed report consistency for every run kind, bounded complete unique hierarchical UTF-8 exports, exact declared file/blob provenance, and manifest/content hash requests on the same bytes. Every finite validator prefix only requests SHA operations. Success from actual transport finish retains its exact caller-bound framing and observed EOF.",
  "consumers": [
    "LeanCage.Host.Application after actual Transport.State.finish",
    "LeanCage.Host.Publication materialization of complete validated output",
    "Later observation provenance and composition delivery"
  ],
  "review": {
    "sameImplementation": "validate_sound unfolds the same Artifacts.validate used by the host engine. actual_transport_artifacts also consumes actual decoder initialization, same run, finish and filesystem-return trajectory.",
    "noConclusionPremise": "No safe manifest, complete artifact plan, precomputed HashesMatch certificate, arbitrary parser transcript or blanket report trust is a top premise. Source declarations, paths, sizes, controls and hash calls are extracted from actual success.",
    "reportKinds": "Run0 and preflight require no artifacts and no entry. Allocated stored reports are byte-equal to REPORT with successful retrieval. Unknown/null observations remain unknown. Bounded terminal controller status is independent of inner guest termination. Profile/runtime bindings are exact caller inputs.",
    "reportPreservation": "The exact parsed JSON and raw report bytes are retained, including extra legal numeric lexemes. Validation failure exposes no partial complete result. Caller must retain already recognized report via Artifacts.knownReport; root owns public projection.",
    "hashPrimitive": "HashSeen witnesses actual op12 request bytes, successful reply and exact 32-byte reply payload in the same execution. HashReplyContract names correctness only of those actual primitive replies; hashSeen_meaning consumes it. No global digest injectivity or whole-plan hash premise.",
    "manifest": "Length is checked before scanning; line size before retention/list creation; sixth token before cons; inodes/declared bytes before append. Canonical decimal/hex/UTF-8 paths, full hierarchy, duplicates, omitted count, declared sizes and both-direction blob references are checked before output.",
    "allocationBounds": "Actual manifest/file/dir/omitted counts and file bytes, path-byte sum, capture/report bounds, checked blob aggregate and digest metadata are proved. splitFields_count and unhexLoop_size bound token/path decoding intermediates. This is actual value/copy accounting, not byte-exact Lean heap layout.",
    "componentPathIdentity": "Structural Char-list splitting preserves Unicode scalars and reconstructs the exact manifest path. It permits root .tmp while rejecting empty/dot/parent/NUL/slash components. Publication uses the same ExportPath.components.",
    "hostileCoverage": "Arbitrary VM bytes and primitive replies remain. Malformed UTF-8, incomplete/trailing manifests, duplicate/conflicting paths, missing/extra/mismatched blobs, mismatched report/capture/storage and primitive failures explicitly reject. Lost prefixes still contain no writes.",
    "nonvacuity": "useful_actual_validation is a closed kernel-checked execution of the complete validator on one full report and useful .tmp export, with actual manifest/content SHA request/reply trajectory. Runtime acceptance also runs full decoder-to-validator fragmentation and run0/preflight/failure cases.",
    "runtimeBoundary": "Linux/runtime/compiler/FFI operations and actual SHA correctness remain explicit per-operation contracts. Later deliveries establish lifetime and observation truth. This is supporting evidence, not a completed M5.2 delivery."
  },
